═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Why a split license
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The platform earns revenue. The standard does not. We deliberately
permissively-license the spec + verifier + CLI so that VAOS receipts
can be adopted as an industry format — by competitors, auditors,
regulators, insurance underwriters — without anyone needing
Sovereign's permission. The platform itself stays proprietary because
that's how we sustain the engineering investment that keeps the
reference implementation correct.

This mirrors the model used by Stripe (Stripe Connect spec public;
platform proprietary), Let's Encrypt (ACME protocol public; platform
proprietary), and Sigstore (open protocol; hosted service operated
by the Linux Foundation).

Contact: spec@sovereignmatrix.agency
